  2A22'   00                    	DB	0
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SEARCH  (/ ? n N)
                                ;
                                ; vi's search on WordMaster's matcher.  What it is NOT: vim searches with a
                                ; REGULAR EXPRESSION and this searches for the literal string typed.  An 8080
                                ; has no room for a regex engine; COMMANDS.md records the deviation.  (WM's own
                                ; search wildcards -- ^A any, ^S separator, ^O not -- are cut from BUF.MAC:
                                ; RDLINE drops control characters, so no pattern could ever hold one.)
                                ;
                                ; Recorded from vim before any of this was written (VIM_SRCH, accept_vi.py):
                                ;   - '/' starts one character PAST the cursor and lands ON the match's first
                                ;     character; '?' finds the last match that ends before the cursor.
                                ;   - 'wrapscan' is on: a search that runs off one end of the file starts
                                ;     again at the other, so '/' on the file's ONLY match finds it again.
                                ;   - 'n' repeats the last search's DIRECTION and 'N' reverses it, so 'n'
                                ;     after a '?' keeps going backward.
                                ;   - An empty pattern ('/' then <CR>) repeats the last pattern.
                                ;   - A count repeats the search: '2/a' is the second match, '15n' fifteen
                                ;     n's.  Not found leaves the cursor exactly where it was, at any count.
                                ;   - The window is placed as 'G' places it -- least scroll when the match is
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-130


                                ;     near, centred when it is far -- which is why this ends in GPLACE.
                                ;
                                ; This replaces a byte-at-a-time search that ran through CHARAT over logical
                                ; offsets: it could only see the resident window (so a match further into a
                                ; paged file did not exist), had no '?' or 'N', and failed silently.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; SUBSTITUTE  (:s  :%s  :N,Ms  and the 'g' flag)
                                ;
                                ; vi's substitute on WordMaster's matcher, so it finds the same LITERAL string
                                ; the search does -- not a regular expression.  COMMANDS.md records that
                                ; deviation for '/' and it is the same one here, which is why nothing below
                                ; honours '&', '\1' or '~'.  The pattern goes into the SEARCH's own buffer
                                ; because vim's ':s' also sets the last search pattern, so 'n' afterwards
                                ; repeats it.
                                ;
                                ; Recorded from vim before any of this was written (VIM_SUBST, accept_vi.py):
                                ;   - ':s' changes the FIRST match on the cursor's line, ':s...g' every match,
                                ;     and the scan goes on PAST the replacement, so a replacement that
                                ;     contains the pattern is not substituted again.
                                ;   - the cursor lands on the first non-blank of the LAST line changed, placed
                                ;     exactly as 'G' places a line -- which is what GZONE before and GPLACE
                                ;     after are for, and it is measured: ':12800,12800s' leaves the last line
                                ;     on row 22 (top 012778) and ':100,105s' leaves line 105 on row 11.
                                ;   - a pattern that is nowhere in the range changes nothing and moves nothing.
                                ;
                                ; A whole substitute is ONE change for 'u': the second UNDBEG, at the first
                                ; match, is what makes the undo's cursor the first match (where vim leaves it)
                                ; rather than the line the ':' was typed on.  A substitute of more than about a
                                ; dozen lines overruns the undo region, which is accepted -- but it SAYS so,
                                ; both when it happens and when 'u' is then pressed.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;EXADDR -- the optional line range before an ex command: '%' (the whole file),
                                ;'N', or 'N,M'.  SRNGF = 0 when there is none, and SRNG2 = 0FFFFH is the last
                                ;line, whatever it turns out to be.  HL comes back on the command letter.
                                ;
                                ; It does NOT consume the blanks after itself: VC_EX's SKIPB does that, so
                                ; ':2,4 s/a/Z/' reads as ':2,4s/a/Z/' the way ex has always taken it.  The one
                                ; place a blank is still refused is INSIDE the range, around the comma
                                ; (':2, 4s'), which ex accepts and this does not -- the comma is read here off
                                ; DE mid-number and skipping there costs more than the position is worth.
  2A23'                         EXADDR:
  2A23'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2A24'   32 0000*              	STA	SRNGF
  2A27'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2A28'   FE 25                 	CPI	'%'
  2A2A'   CA 2A53'              	JZ	EXA_AL
  2A2D'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE walks the line, HL takes the number
  2A2E'   CD 2A68'              	CALL	EXNUM
  2A31'   DA 2A51'              	JC	EXA_NO
  2A34'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRNG1
  2A37'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRNG2		; 'N' alone is the single line 'N,N'
  2A3A'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  2A3B'   FE 2C                 	CPI	','
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-131


  2A3D'   C2 2A4A'              	JNZ	EXA_YS
  2A40'   13                    	INX	D
  2A41'   CD 2A68'              	CALL	EXNUM
  2A44'   DA 2A51'              	JC	EXA_NO		; ',' with no number: not a range at all
  2A47'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRNG2
  2A4A'                         EXA_YS:
  2A4A'   EB                    	XCHG
  2A4B'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2A4D'   32 0000*              	STA	SRNGF
  2A50'   C9                    	RET
  2A51'                         EXA_NO:
  2A51'   EB                    	XCHG
  2A52'   C9                    	RET
  2A53'                         EXA_AL:
  2A53'   23                    	INX	H
  2A54'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2A55'   21 0001               	LXI	H,1
  2A58'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRNG1
  2A5B'   21 FFFF               	LXI	H,0FFFFH
  2A5E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SRNG2
  2A61'   E1                    	POP	H
  2A62'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2A64'   32 0000*              	STA	SRNGF
  2A67'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;EXNUM -- a decimal number at DE -> HL, DE left past it.  CY when there is no
                                ;digit there at all.
  2A68'                         EXNUM:
  2A68'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  2A69'   D6 30                 	SUI	'0'
  2A6B'   D8                    	RC
  2A6C'   FE 0A                 	CPI	10
  2A6E'   3F                    	CMC
  2A6F'   D8                    	RC
  2A70'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0
  2A73'                         EXN_LP:
  2A73'   1A                    	LDAX	D
  2A74'   D6 30                 	SUI	'0'
  2A76'   DA 2A90'              	JC	EXN_DN
  2A79'   FE 0A                 	CPI	10
  2A7B'   D2 2A90'              	JNC	EXN_DN
  2A7E'   13                    	INX	D
  2A7F'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  2A80'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  2A81'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0		; BC = the digit
  2A83'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  2A84'   54                    	MOV	D,H
  2A85'   5D                    	MOV	E,L
  2A86'   29                    	DAD	H		; *2
  2A87'   29                    	DAD	H		; *4
  2A88'   19                    	DAD	D		; *5
  2A89'   29                    	DAD	H		; *10
  2A8A'   D1                    	POP	D
  2A8B'   09                    	DAD	B
  2A8C'   C1                    	POP	B
  2A8D'   C3 2A73'              	JMP	EXN_LP
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-132


  2A90'                         EXN_DN:
  2A90'   B7                    	ORA	A		; CY clear: there was a number
  2A91'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;EX_S -- ':s': the delimiter, the pattern, the replacement, an optional 'g'.
  2A92'                         EX_S:
  2A92'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2A93'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2A94'   CA 2AD6'              	JZ	SUBNOP		; ':s' alone -- repeating the last one is not
                                				;   built (COMMANDS.md)
  2A97'   32 0000*              	STA	SDELIM
  2A9A'   23                    	INX	H
  2A9B'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCHST
  2A9E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCMAX		; the pattern's capacity is BUF.MAC's to state
  2AA1'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  2AA2'   CD 2ADC'              	CALL	SCOPY
  2AA5'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  2AA6'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2AA7'   CA 2AD6'              	JZ	SUBNOP		; ':s//x/' -- an empty pattern matches nothing
  2AAA'   32 0000*              	STA	SRCHBF		; WM's RDSTR layout: the length below the string
  2AAD'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2AAF'   32 0000*              	STA	SHAVE		; 'n' repeats it, as after a '/'
  2AB2'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SREPL
  2AB5'   0E 24                 	MVI	C,SREPMX
  2AB7'   CD 2ADC'              	CALL	SCOPY
  2ABA'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  2ABB'   32 0000*              	STA	SREPLN
  2ABE'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2ABF'   32 0000*              	STA	SGFLAG
  2AC2'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2AC3'   FE 67                 	CPI	'g'
  2AC5'   C2 2ACE'              	JNZ	EX_SG
  2AC8'   23                    	INX	H
  2AC9'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2ACB'   32 0000*              	STA	SGFLAG
  2ACE'                         EX_SG:
  2ACE'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2ACF'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2AD0'   C2 283D'              	JNZ	EX_TRL		; 'Trailing chars: ' -- vim's, shortened
  2AD3'   C3 2AFC'              	JMP	SUBGO
  2AD6'                         SUBNOP:
  2AD6'   21 2905'              	LXI	H,SNOPAT
  2AD9'   C3 284B'              	JMP	EXERR
                                
                                ;SCOPY -- the text at HL up to SDELIM (or the line's end) into [DE], C its
                                ;capacity: B = how many were taken, HL past the delimiter, and [DE] is left
                                ;0-terminated as WM's RDSTR leaves a string.
  2ADC'                         SCOPY:
  2ADC'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0
  2ADE'                         SCP_LP:
  2ADE'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  2ADF'   B9                    	CMP	C
  2AE0'   D2 2AF9'              	JNC	SCP_DN		; full: what is left stays on the line, and so
                                				;   comes back as trailing characters
  2AE3'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2AE4'   B7                    	ORA	A
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-133


  2AE5'   CA 2AF9'              	JZ	SCP_DN		; the line ended: no closing delimiter wanted
  2AE8'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2AE9'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SDELIM
  2AEC'   BE                    	CMP	M
  2AED'   E1                    	POP	H
  2AEE'   CA 2AF8'              	JZ	SCP_SK
  2AF1'   12                    	STAX	D
  2AF2'   13                    	INX	D
  2AF3'   23                    	INX	H
  2AF4'   04                    	INR	B
  2AF5'   C3 2ADE'              	JMP	SCP_LP
  2AF8'                         SCP_SK:
  2AF8'   23                    	INX	H
  2AF9'                         SCP_DN:
  2AF9'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2AFA'   12                    	STAX	D
  2AFB'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SUBGO -- run the substitute.  GZONE comes first, before anything moves: the
                                ;landing is placed as 'G' places a line, and GPLACE measures it against the
                                ;screen's top line as it was when the command was typed.
  2AFC'                         SUBGO:
  2AFC'   CD 1405'              	CALL	GZONE
  2AFF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	LNDLT
  2B02'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SLDLTS		; the walk moves the cursor; a substitute that
  2B05'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SOFFS		;   finds nothing puts both back, as the
  2B08'   CD 0448'              	CALL	FPSTO		;   search's SN_BAD does
  2B0B'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2B0C'   32 0000*              	STA	SANY
  2B0F'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0
  2B12'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SBACK
  2B15'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRNGF
  2B18'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2B19'   CA 2B2B'              	JZ	SUB_1L
                                	;--- ':N,Ms' / ':%s': to the range's first line, then walk it ---
  2B1C'   CD 23CB'              	CALL	EXRNG		; SLINES = the lines in the range
  2B1F'   DA 2BA7'              	JC	SUBBAD
  2B22'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SRNG1
  2B25'   CD 135E'              	CALL	GOLN
  2B28'   C3 2B31'              	JMP	SUBLP
  2B2B'                         SUB_1L:
  2B2B'   21 0001               	LXI	H,1
  2B2E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SLINES
  2B31'                         SUBLP:
  2B31'   CD 2BAD'              	CALL	SUBLIN		; A = 1 when this line changed
  2B34'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2B35'   CA 2B43'              	JZ	SUB_NX
  2B38'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2B3A'   32 0000*              	STA	SANY
  2B3D'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0
  2B40'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SBACK		; the cursor is ON the last line changed
  2B43'                         SUB_NX:
  2B43'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SLINES
  2B46'   2B                    	DCX	H
  2B47'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SLINES
  2B4A'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-134


  2B4B'   B5                    	ORA	L
  2B4C'   CA 2B6A'              	JZ	SUBDON		; the range is spent
  2B4F'   21 0001               	LXI	H,1
  2B52'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2B53'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MVLIND		; the next line, paging with it
  2B56'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SANY
  2B59'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2B5A'   CA 2B64'              	JZ	SUB_AE		; nothing changed yet: nothing to count from
  2B5D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SBACK
  2B60'   23                    	INX	H
  2B61'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SBACK		; every step taken after the last change has
                                				;   to be walked back at the end -- including
                                				;   this one, when it lands past the last line
  2B64'                         SUB_AE:
  2B64'   CD 0BFA'              	CALL	ATEOF
  2B67'   D2 2B31'              	JNC	SUBLP		; ... unless that ran off the end of the file
  2B6A'                         SUBDON:
  2B6A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CLRCNT		; the walk left the count and direction set
  2B6D'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SANY
  2B70'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2B71'   CA 2B8F'              	JZ	SUBNFD
  2B74'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2B76'   32 0000*              	STA	MODF		; the text changed, so ':w' has work to do.  NOT
                                				;   MARKMOD: that also sets DOTCHG, and '.' does
                                				;   not repeat a substitute in vim either (that
                                				;   is '&', which is not built)
  2B79'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SBACK
  2B7C'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2B7D'   B5                    	ORA	L
  2B7E'   CA 2B89'              	JZ	SUB_PL
  2B81'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH
  2B83'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MVLIND		; back to the last line changed
  2B86'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CLRCNT
  2B89'                         SUB_PL:
  2B89'   CD 141D'              	CALL	GPLACE		; the landing: first non-blank, placed as 'G'
  2B8C'   C3 08AE'              	JMP	SETFUL		; GPLACE asks for R_MOVE when the target is
                                				;   which rewrote the line under the cursor.
                                				; And that repaint is why a substitute too big
                                				;   for the undo does NOT say so here: EXMSG
                                				;   draws the bottom row there and then, and
                                				;   the full paint this needs takes the status
                                				;   row back (SCRN.MAC says so itself).  'u'
                                				;   carries the message instead -- UNDWHY = 2,
                                				;   at the moment the reader asks for the undo
                                				;   and can still act on the answer.
  2B8F'                         SUBNFD:
  2B8F'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SOFFS
  2B92'   CD 03EF'              	CALL	BACKTO
  2B95'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SLDLTS
  2B98'   22 0000*              	SHLD	LNDLT		; nothing changed: the row the cursor was on
  2B9B'   21 28D5'              	LXI	H,SNOTFD
  2B9E'   CD 284B'              	CALL	EXERR
  2BA1'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCHST
  2BA4'   C3 2846'              	JMP	EXOUT		; 'Pattern not found: ' and the pattern
  2BA7'                         SUBBAD:
  2BA7'   21 28C3'              	LXI	H,SNOT
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-135


  2BAA'   C3 2840'              	JMP	EXERT
                                
                                ;SUBLIN -- the substitute on the cursor's line: the first match, or every match
                                ;when 'g' was given.  A = 1 when the line changed.  The cursor is left at the
                                ;line's start either way, so the walk to the next line always starts from one.
                                ;Every offset is re-derived from the cursor after each change, never held
                                ;across one: an insert can page (':%s/0/ZZ/' grows a 100 K file by 12800
                                ;bytes) and paging shifts every logical offset in the window.
  2BAD'                         SUBLIN:
  2BAD'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2BAE'   32 0000*              	STA	SLCHG
  2BB1'   CD 2C2C'              	CALL	SUBBOL
  2BB4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	RGET0		; the line has to be RESIDENT before CEND can
  2BB7'                         SUBL_R:				;   find its end: the pager keeps the CURSOR in
  2BB7'   CD 0000*              	CALL	RGET		;   the window, not the whole line it sits on,
  2BBA'   DA 2BC2'              	JC	SUBL_L		;   and EOLNL only ever scans resident text --
  2BBD'   FE 0A                 	CPI	LF		;   so a line straddling the resident end came
  2BBF'   C2 2BB7'              	JNZ	SUBL_R		;   out short and went unsubstituted (line 179
                                				;   of the 66 K indented file, which starts at
                                				;   byte 2047).  RGET pages through NEEDIN, as
                                				;   every other line reader here does.
  2BC2'                         SUBL_L:
                                	;--- the scan window: the cursor to the line's content end ---
  2BC2'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CUROFF
  2BC5'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2BC6'   CD 1A00'              	CALL	CEND
  2BC9'   D1                    	POP	D
  2BCA'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = the bytes left on the line
  2BCD'   23                    	INX	H		; FWDCNT's own arithmetic, inline: the span it
  2BCE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		;   would measure, plus one, less the pattern.
  2BD1'   7C                    	MOV	A,H		;   (FWDCNT needs a real pointer pair and this
  2BD2'   B7                    	ORA	A		;   span is a line, not a pair.)
  2BD3'   FA 2C25'              	JM	SUBL_D		; what is left is shorter than the pattern
  2BD6'   44                    	MOV	B,H
  2BD7'   4D                    	MOV	C,L		; BC = the start positions a match can take
  2BD8'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCHST
  2BDB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND		; with the gap at the cursor, the line runs
  2BDE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MATCHF		;   forward from GAPEND
  2BE1'   DA 2C25'              	JC	SUBL_D
  2BE4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		; MATCHF ends past the match; back to its start
  2BE7'   EB                    	XCHG
  2BE8'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND
  2BEB'   EB                    	XCHG
  2BEC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = how far into the scan the match is
  2BEF'   EB                    	XCHG
  2BF0'   D5                    	PUSH	D		; CUROFF does NOT keep DE (it reads TXTBEG into
  2BF1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CUROFF		;   it), so the delta goes on the stack
  2BF4'   D1                    	POP	D
  2BF5'   19                    	DAD	D		; ... and so the match's logical offset
  2BF6'   CD 0000*              	CALL	GOTO
                                	;--- the first change of the whole substitute re-arms the undo, so 'u'
                                	;    lands on the first match, which is where vim leaves it ---
  2BF9'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SANY
  2BFC'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2BFD'   C2 2C0A'              	JNZ	SUBL_C
  2C00'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SLCHG
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-136


  2C03'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2C04'   C2 2C0A'              	JNZ	SUBL_C
  2C07'   CD 0000*              	CALL	UNDHER		; the cursor snapshot only: UNDBEG would re-run
                                				;   UNDGRW mid-command, and growing the region
                                				;   where a primitive can see it corrupts the
                                				;   gap ('COPY ERR')
  2C0A'                         SUBL_C:
  2C0A'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCHBF
  2C0D'   6F                    	MOV	L,A
  2C0E'   26 00                 	MVI	H,0
  2C10'   CD 0000*              	CALL	DELFWD		; the match goes
  2C13'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SREPLN	; ... and the replacement takes its place, the
  2C16'   CD 0000*              	CALL	INSSTR		;   way WM splices one: the length byte with
                                				;   its string above it, 'u' capture included
  2C19'                         SUBL_I:
  2C19'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2C1B'   32 0000*              	STA	SLCHG
  2C1E'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SGFLAG
  2C21'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2C22'   C2 2BC2'              	JNZ	SUBL_L		; 'g': on from PAST the replacement
  2C25'                         SUBL_D:
  2C25'   CD 2C2C'              	CALL	SUBBOL
  2C28'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SLCHG
  2C2B'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SUBBOL -- the cursor to the start of the line it is on.
  2C2C'                         SUBBOL:
  2C2C'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CUROFF
  2C2F'   CD 0697'              	CALL	BOL
  2C32'   C3 0000*              	JMP	GOTO
                                
                                ;VC_SRCH -- '/' and '?': read the pattern, then search.  C is the key, which
                                ; is both the prompt character and the direction.
  2C35'                         VC_SRCH:
  2C35'   CD 0871'              	CALL	SETMOV
  2C38'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  2C39'   CD 079C'              	CALL	GETCNT
  2C3C'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCNT
  2C3F'   C1                    	POP	B
  2C40'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  2C41'   FE 2F                 	CPI	'/'
  2C43'   3E 00                 	MVI	A,0
  2C45'   CA 2C4A'              	JZ	VS_DIR
  2C48'   3E FF                 	MVI	A,0FFH		; '?' -- backward
  2C4A'                         VS_DIR:
  2C4A'   32 0000*              	STA	SDIR
  2C4D'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCHST	; the line is read straight into the pattern
  2C50'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCMAX		; its capacity is BUF.MAC's to state
  2C53'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  2C54'   CD 216F'              	CALL	RDLINE
  2C57'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2C58'   C0                    	RNZ			; cancelled: nothing happens at all
  2C59'   3A 0000*              	LDA	RLLEN
  2C5C'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2C5D'   CA 2C72'              	JZ	VS_OLD		; an empty line repeats the last pattern --
                                				;   RDLINE stored nothing, so it is still there
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-137


  2C60'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
  2C61'   16 00                 	MVI	D,0
  2C63'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCHST
  2C66'   19                    	DAD	D
  2C67'   36 00                 	MVI	M,0		; 0-terminated, and the length below it:
  2C69'   7B                    	MOV	A,E
  2C6A'   32 0000*              	STA	SRCHBF		;   WM's RDSTR layout, built by hand
  2C6D'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2C6F'   32 0000*              	STA	SHAVE
  2C72'                         VS_OLD:
  2C72'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SHAVE
  2C75'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2C76'   CA 2C82'              	JZ	VS_NOP		; '/' <CR> with nothing ever searched for
  2C79'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIR
  2C7C'   32 0000*              	STA	SDIRE
  2C7F'   C3 2CAB'              	JMP	SRCHN
  2C82'                         VS_NOP:
  2C82'   21 2905'              	LXI	H,SNOPAT
  2C85'   C3 284B'              	JMP	EXERR
                                
                                ;VC_N / VCB_N -- 'n' repeats the last search, 'N' reverses its direction.
  2C88'                         VC_N:
  2C88'   CD 0871'              	CALL	SETMOV
  2C8B'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIR
  2C8E'   C3 2C98'              	JMP	VN_GO
  2C91'                         VCB_N:
  2C91'   CD 0871'              	CALL	SETMOV
  2C94'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIR
  2C97'   2F                    	CMA			; the other way: 0 <-> FFH
  2C98'                         VN_GO:
  2C98'   32 0000*              	STA	SDIRE
  2C9B'   CD 079C'              	CALL	GETCNT
  2C9E'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCNT
  2CA1'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SHAVE
  2CA4'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2CA5'   CA 2C82'              	JZ	VS_NOP
  2CA8'   C3 2CAB'              	JMP	SRCHN
                                
                                ;SRCHN -- the count, one whole-file search each.  Not found at ANY repeat
                                ; leaves the cursor where the command started, as vim does, and says so; the
                                ; message wants the screen left alone, which is what EXERR's R_MOVE is for.
  2CAB'                         SRCHN:
  2CAB'   CD 1405'              	CALL	GZONE		; the screen's top line, before the cursor moves
  2CAE'   CD 07C5'              	CALL	BRKON		; where it started (the sweep moves the cursor
                                				;   with PUTCUR, which does not maintain LNDLT;
                                				;   GOTO does), and an ESC may stop it
  2CB1'                         SN_LP:
  2CB1'   CD 2CE6'              	CALL	SRCHGO
  2CB4'   DA 2CD1'              	JC	SN_BAD
  2CB7'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCNT
  2CBA'   2B                    	DCX	H
  2CBB'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCNT
  2CBE'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2CBF'   B5                    	ORA	L
  2CC0'   C2 2CB1'              	JNZ	SN_LP
  2CC3'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CLRCNT		; the sweep left CMDCNT wide open (and DIRFLG
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-138


                                				;   backward): WM clears both per command
  2CC6'   CD 0802'              	CALL	BRKOFF
  2CC9'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2CCB'   32 0000*              	STA	GPKEEP		; land on the match, not the first non-blank
  2CCE'   C3 141D'              	JMP	GPLACE		; (which sets LNDLT itself)
  2CD1'                         SN_BAD:
  2CD1'   CD 0802'              	CALL	BRKOFF
  2CD4'   DA 081A'              	JC	BRKBAK		; stopped, which is not the same as not found
  2CD7'   CD 080D'              	CALL	RSTPL		; nothing moved: the row the cursor was on
  2CDA'   21 28D5'              	LXI	H,SNOTFD
  2CDD'   CD 284B'              	CALL	EXERR
  2CE0'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SRCHST
  2CE3'   C3 2846'              	JMP	EXOUT		; 'Pattern not found: ' and the pattern
                                
                                ;SRCHGO -- one search of the whole file, wrapping once: from the cursor to the
                                ; end in SDIRE's direction, paging as WM's find pages, then the rest of the
                                ; file READ where it lies (SCAN) and the window moved once, to the match --
                                ; not paged round the whole file a second time (issue #35).  CY = the pattern
                                ; is nowhere in the file, or an ESC stopped it (BRKQ says which); the cursor
                                ; is then at an end of the file, and SRCHN puts it back.
  2CE6'                         SRCHGO:
  2CE6'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SGPOS
  2CE9'   CD 0448'              	CALL	FPSTO		; where this one starts: the wrapped pass ends
  2CEC'   CD 2F3C'              	CALL	SRCHW		;   there
  2CEF'   D0                    	RNC
  2CF0'   CD 0806'              	CALL	BRKQ
  2CF3'   D8                    	RC			; stopped: no second pass
  2CF4'   CD 2D01'              	CALL	SCAN
  2CF7'   D8                    	RC
  2CF8'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SCHIT
  2CFB'   CD 03EF'              	CALL	BACKTO		; to the match: one move, as a mark jump
  2CFE'   C3 0806'              	JMP	BRKQ		; CY: stopped on the way there
                                
                                ;SCAN -- the wrapped pass, without moving the window: the records above it,
                                ; the window, then the records below it, through SECBUF in file order (SCNEXT).
                                ; The last bytes of each piece, a pattern less one, are kept just below
                                ; SECBUF, so a match that straddles two pieces is seen whole there.  '/'
                                ; wants the FIRST match in the file and stops reading once a match could only
                                ; start past SGPOS -- the first pass found nothing there.  '?' wants the LAST,
                                ; so it reads to the end, but skips the records that end before SCLIM: the
                                ; first pass found nothing that ends before SGPOS.  NC: SCHIT = the match's
                                ; file position.  CY: there is none, or an ESC stopped it.
  2D01'                         SCAN:
  2D01'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2D02'   32 0000*              	STA	SCFND
  2D05'   32 0000*              	STA	SCCRY
  2D08'   32 0000*              	STA	SCPH		; the records above the window first
  2D0B'   32 0002*              	STA	SCPOS+2
  2D0E'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0
  2D11'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2D14'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCPOS
  2D17'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCHBF
  2D1A'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
  2D1B'   16 00                 	MVI	D,0		; DE = the pattern's length
  2D1D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SGPOS
  2D20'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIRE
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-139


  2D23'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D24'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SGPOS+2
  2D27'   FA 2D30'              	JM	SC_BK
  2D2A'   19                    	DAD	D		; '/': SGPOS + the length
  2D2B'   CE 00                 	ACI	0
  2D2D'   C3 2D3A'              	JMP	SC_LIM
  2D30'                         SC_BK:
  2D30'   42                    	MOV	B,D
  2D31'   CD 13B2'              	CALL	SUB24		; '?': SGPOS - the length (0 if that is less)
  2D34'   D2 2D3A'              	JNC	SC_LIM
  2D37'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2D38'   67                    	MOV	H,A
  2D39'   6F                    	MOV	L,A
  2D3A'                         SC_LIM:
  2D3A'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCLIM
  2D3D'   32 0002*              	STA	SCLIM+2
  2D40'                         SC_LP:
  2D40'   3A 0000*              	LDA	BRKARM
  2D43'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D44'   C4 07DF'              	CNZ	BRKTST		; an ESC, as CNTTST looks for one
  2D47'   CD 0806'              	CALL	BRKQ
  2D4A'   D8                    	RC
  2D4B'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIRE
  2D4E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D4F'   FA 2D6B'              	JM	SC_RD		; '?' reads to the end
  2D52'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCFND
  2D55'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D56'   C0                    	RNZ			; '/': the first is all it wants (NC)
  2D57'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCLIM
  2D5A'   EB                    	XCHG
  2D5B'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SCLIM+2
  2D5E'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  2D5F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCPOS
  2D62'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SCPOS+2
  2D65'   CD 13B2'              	CALL	SUB24		; NC: no match can start at SGPOS or before
  2D68'   D2 2D78'              	JNC	SC_END		;   from here on
  2D6B'                         SC_RD:
  2D6B'   CD 2E1B'              	CALL	SCNEXT		; SECBUF = the next piece, A = its length
  2D6E'   DA 2D78'              	JC	SC_END		; the file has run out
  2D71'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D72'   C4 2D7E'              	CNZ	SCMAT
  2D75'   C3 2D40'              	JMP	SC_LP
  2D78'                         SC_END:
  2D78'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCFND
  2D7B'   D6 01                 	SUI	1		; CY iff there is none
  2D7D'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SCMAT -- look for the pattern in the A bytes in SECBUF and the carry below
                                ; it, then keep the last of them as the carry and move SCPOS past them.
  2D7E'                         SCMAT:
  2D7E'   4F                    	MOV	C,A
  2D7F'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0
  2D81'   C5                    	PUSH	B		; the length of the piece
  2D82'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCHBF
  2D85'   67                    	MOV	H,A
  2D86'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCCRY
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-140


  2D89'   81                    	ADD	C		; the carry and the piece
  2D8A'   94                    	SUB	H
  2D8B'   DA 2DE2'              	JC	SCM_NO		; shorter than the pattern
  2D8E'   3C                    	INR	A
  2D8F'   4F                    	MOV	C,A		; BC = the places a match may start at
  2D90'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCHST
  2D93'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIRE
  2D96'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2D97'   FA 2DB4'              	JM	SCM_BK
  2D9A'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCCRY		; '/': the first, from the carry's first byte
  2D9D'   2F                    	CMA
  2D9E'   6F                    	MOV	L,A
  2D9F'   26 FF                 	MVI	H,0FFH
  2DA1'   23                    	INX	H		; HL = - the carry
  2DA2'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  2DA3'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  2DA6'   19                    	DAD	D
  2DA7'   D1                    	POP	D
  2DA8'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MATCHF
  2DAB'   DA 2DE2'              	JC	SCM_NO
  2DAE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		; MATCHF ends past the match
  2DB1'   C3 2DC5'              	JMP	SCM_HI
  2DB4'                         SCM_BK:
  2DB4'   E1                    	POP	H		; '?': the last, back from the piece's end
  2DB5'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2DB6'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  2DB7'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  2DBA'   19                    	DAD	D
  2DBB'   D1                    	POP	D
  2DBC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		; the last place one can start
  2DBF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MATCHB
  2DC2'   DA 2DE2'              	JC	SCM_NO
  2DC5'                         SCM_HI:
  2DC5'   EB                    	XCHG			; DE = the match, in SECBUF or below it
  2DC6'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCPOS
  2DC9'   19                    	DAD	D
  2DCA'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SCPOS+2
  2DCD'   CE 00                 	ACI	0
  2DCF'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  2DD2'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0
  2DD4'   CD 13B2'              	CALL	SUB24		; its file position
  2DD7'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCHIT
  2DDA'   32 0002*              	STA	SCHIT+2
  2DDD'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2DDF'   32 0000*              	STA	SCFND
  2DE2'                         SCM_NO:
  2DE2'   C1                    	POP	B		; BC = the piece's length
  2DE3'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  2DE4'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCCRY
  2DE7'   81                    	ADD	C
  2DE8'   5F                    	MOV	E,A		; the carry and the piece
  2DE9'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SRCHBF
  2DEC'   3D                    	DCR	A		; ... of which a pattern less one is kept
  2DED'   BB                    	CMP	E
  2DEE'   DA 2DF2'              	JC	SCM_T
  2DF1'   7B                    	MOV	A,E
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-141


  2DF2'                         SCM_T:
  2DF2'   32 0000*              	STA	SCCRY
  2DF5'   5F                    	MOV	E,A
  2DF6'   16 00                 	MVI	D,0		; DE = the new carry
  2DF8'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  2DFB'   09                    	DAD	B
  2DFC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; the bytes it keeps
  2DFF'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2E00'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,SECBUF
  2E03'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; where they go
  2E06'   42                    	MOV	B,D
  2E07'   4B                    	MOV	C,E
  2E08'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E09'   E1                    	POP	H
  2E0A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY		; (down, so a forward copy is safe)
  2E0D'   D1                    	POP	D		; the piece's length
                                ;SCADV -- SCPOS += DE.
  2E0E'                         SCADV:
  2E0E'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCPOS
  2E11'   19                    	DAD	D
  2E12'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCPOS
  2E15'   D0                    	RNC
  2E16'   21 0002*              	LXI	H,SCPOS+2
  2E19'   34                    	INR	M
  2E1A'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SCNEXT -- the next piece of the file into SECBUF: A = its length, which is 0
                                ; for a record skipped.  CY: the file has run out.  SCPH is what it is in:
                                ; 0 the records above the window, 1 the window before the gap, 2 after it,
                                ; 3 VIBACKUP.$$$ (top down), 4 the source below, 5 nothing left.
  2E1B'                         SCNEXT:
  2E1B'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCPH
  2E1E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2E1F'   CA 2E31'              	JZ	SN_AB
  2E22'   FE 03                 	CPI	3
  2E24'   DA 2E5F'              	JC	SN_GP
  2E27'   CA 2ED5'              	JZ	SN_BAK
  2E2A'   FE 04                 	CPI	4
  2E2C'   CA 2EEF'              	JZ	SN_SRC
  2E2F'   37                    	STC
  2E30'   C9                    	RET
  2E31'                         SN_AB:
  2E31'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  2E34'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E35'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCIX
  2E38'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16
  2E3B'   CA 2E49'              	JZ	SN_W0		; all of them read: the window
  2E3E'   23                    	INX	H
  2E3F'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2E42'   2B                    	DCX	H
  2E43'   AF                    	XRA	A		; above the window
  2E44'   CD 2F06'              	CALL	SN_REC
  2E47'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2E48'   C9                    	RET
  2E49'                         SN_W0:
  2E49'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTBEG
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-142


  2E4C'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E4D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG
  2E50'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2E52'                         SN_PH:				; phase A, from DE up to HL
  2E52'   32 0000*              	STA	SCPH
  2E55'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCEND
  2E58'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E59'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2E5C'   C3 2E1B'              	JMP	SCNEXT
  2E5F'                         SN_GP:				; the window: up to 128 bytes of it, copied
  2E5F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCIX
  2E62'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E63'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCEND
  2E66'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBHD		; HL = what is left of this part
  2E69'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2E6A'   B5                    	ORA	L
  2E6B'   CA 2E90'              	JZ	SN_GPX
  2E6E'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2E6F'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2E70'   C2 2E79'              	JNZ	SN_128
  2E73'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  2E74'   FE 81                 	CPI	81H
  2E76'   DA 2E7C'              	JC	SN_GPN
  2E79'                         SN_128:
  2E79'   21 0080               	LXI	H,80H
  2E7C'                         SN_GPN:
  2E7C'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2E7D'   44                    	MOV	B,H
  2E7E'   4D                    	MOV	C,L
  2E7F'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E80'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2E81'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SECBUF
  2E84'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MEMCPY
  2E87'   E1                    	POP	H
  2E88'   C1                    	POP	B
  2E89'   09                    	DAD	B
  2E8A'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2E8D'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  2E8E'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2E8F'   C9                    	RET
  2E90'                         SN_GPX:
  2E90'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SCPH
  2E93'   FE 02                 	CPI	2
  2E95'   CA 2EA4'              	JZ	SN_BLW
  2E98'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND
  2E9B'   EB                    	XCHG
  2E9C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	TXTEND
  2E9F'   3E 02                 	MVI	A,2
  2EA1'   C3 2E52'              	JMP	SN_PH
  2EA4'                         SN_BLW:				; below the window: VIBACKUP.$$$ if it holds
  2EA4'   3A 0000*              	LDA	BAKRDY		;   anything, as RDIN reads it first
  2EA7'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2EA8'   CA 2EBE'              	JZ	SN_S0
  2EAB'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	BAKPOS
  2EAE'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2EAF'   B5                    	ORA	L
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-143


  2EB0'   CA 2EBE'              	JZ	SN_S0
  2EB3'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2EB6'   3E 03                 	MVI	A,3
  2EB8'   32 0000*              	STA	SCPH
  2EBB'   C3 2E1B'              	JMP	SCNEXT
  2EBE'                         SN_S0:				; then the source, from where it is read to
  2EBE'   3A 005B               	LDA	5BH
  2EC1'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2EC2'   3E 05                 	MVI	A,5
  2EC4'   CA 2ECF'              	JZ	SN_END
  2EC7'   2A 007E               	LHLD	7EH
  2ECA'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2ECD'   3E 04                 	MVI	A,4
  2ECF'                         SN_END:
  2ECF'   32 0000*              	STA	SCPH
  2ED2'   C3 2E1B'              	JMP	SCNEXT
  2ED5'                         SN_BAK:
  2ED5'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCIX
  2ED8'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  2ED9'   B5                    	ORA	L
  2EDA'   CA 2EBE'              	JZ	SN_S0		; record 0 read
  2EDD'   2B                    	DCX	H
  2EDE'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2EE1'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1
  2EE3'   CD 2F06'              	CALL	SN_REC
  2EE6'   D0                    	RNC
  2EE7'   21 0000               	LXI	H,0		; a ^Z: the stack ends there (RDIN's IOEOF)
  2EEA'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2EED'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2EEE'   C9                    	RET
  2EEF'                         SN_SRC:
  2EEF'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCIX
  2EF2'   23                    	INX	H
  2EF3'   22 0000*              	SHLD	SCIX
  2EF6'   2B                    	DCX	H
  2EF7'   3E 02                 	MVI	A,2
  2EF9'   CD 2F06'              	CALL	SN_REC
  2EFC'   D0                    	RNC
  2EFD'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW		; a ^Z or no record: the end of the file
  2EFE'   3E 05                 	MVI	A,5
  2F00'   32 0000*              	STA	SCPH
  2F03'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  2F04'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2F05'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SN_REC -- SCNREC (record HL, kind A), unless it is a '?' record that ends
                                ; before SCLIM, which is skipped: SCPOS moves past it and the carry goes (a
                                ; record is 128 bytes until the last, and that one is never skipped).
  2F06'                         SN_REC:
  2F06'   F5                    	PUSH	PSW
  2F07'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2F08'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIRE
  2F0B'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2F0C'   F2 2F37'              	JP	SN_RD		; '/' never skips
  2F0F'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCPOS
  2F12'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-144


  2F15'   19                    	DAD	D
  2F16'   EB                    	XCHG
  2F17'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SCPOS+2
  2F1A'   CE 00                 	ACI	0
  2F1C'   47                    	MOV	B,A		; B:DE = past this record
  2F1D'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	SCLIM
  2F20'   3A 0002*              	LDA	SCLIM+2
  2F23'   CD 13B2'              	CALL	SUB24		; NC: it ends at SCLIM or before
  2F26'   DA 2F37'              	JC	SN_RD
  2F29'   E1                    	POP	H
  2F2A'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  2F2B'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2F2C'   32 0000*              	STA	SCCRY
  2F2F'   11 0080               	LXI	D,80H
  2F32'   CD 2E0E'              	CALL	SCADV
  2F35'   AF                    	XRA	A		; nothing to look at, NC
  2F36'   C9                    	RET
  2F37'                         SN_RD:
  2F37'   E1                    	POP	H
  2F38'   F1                    	POP	PSW
  2F39'   C3 0000*              	JMP	SCNREC
                                
                                ;SRCHW -- WM FINDA (WM 1943): the file from the cursor on, one resident
                                ; window at a time.  A miss moves the cursor to that window's edge and pages
                                ; one step (SCRLST), so the search runs off the window and through the file;
                                ; CY when the file runs out.  PAGESTP only pages while the count is unspent,
                                ; so the sweep opens CMDCNT wide, as MVLMAX does.  WM's FINDA then puts the
                                ; cursor exactly at the file's end (WM 1949); nothing here needs that -- the
                                ; caller reads the rest of the file or restores the cursor outright.
  2F3C'                         SRCHW:
  2F3C'   3A 0000*              	LDA	SDIRE
  2F3F'   32 0000*              	STA	DIRFLG
  2F42'   21 FFFF               	LXI	H,0FFFFH
  2F45'   22 0000*              	SHLD	CMDCNT
  2F48'   AF                    	XRA	A
  2F49'   32 0000*              	STA	AUXCNT
  2F4C'                         SW_LP:
  2F4C'   CD 0806'              	CALL	BRKQ		; an ESC spent the count, here or on the way to
  2F4F'   D8                    	RC			;   the wrapped pass: SCRLST no longer pages
  2F50'   CD 2F5C'              	CALL	SRCH1
  2F53'   D0                    	RNC
  2F54'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SCRLST
  2F57'   D2 2F4C'              	JNC	SW_LP
  2F5A'   37                    	STC
  2F5B'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;SRCH1 -- WM FINDB (WM 1984) without its RDSTR: one search inside the
                                ; resident window, DIRFLG picking the direction.  CY = not in this window; on
                                ; a hit the cursor is ON the match's first character.
  2F5C'                         SRCH1:
  2F5C'   11 0000*              	LXI	D,SRCHST
  2F5F'   3A 0000*              	LDA	DIRFLG
  2F62'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2F63'   FA 2F80'              	JM	SR1_BK
  2F66'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,GAPEND
  2F69'   CD 0000*              	CALL	FWDCNT
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-145


  2F6C'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPEND		; WM loads the pointer BEFORE testing the
  2F6F'   D8                    	RC			;   carry: a miss still has to leave HL a
                                				;   real text address, because SCRLST puts
                                				;   the cursor there on the way to paging
  2F70'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  2F71'   B1                    	ORA	C
  2F72'   37                    	STC
  2F73'   C8                    	RZ			; no room for a match even before the skip
  2F74'   0B                    	DCX	B		; vim's '/' starts one character PAST the
  2F75'   23                    	INX	H		;   cursor, so the character under it can
                                				;   never be the one that matches
  2F76'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MATCHF
  2F79'   D8                    	RC
  2F7A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		; MATCHF ends PAST the match; vi lands on it
  2F7D'   C3 0000*              	JMP	PUTCUR
  2F80'                         SR1_BK:
  2F80'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TXTBEG
  2F83'   CD 0000*              	CALL	FWDCNT
  2F86'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	GAPBEG		; (as above: the pointer, then the carry)
  2F89'   D8                    	RC
  2F8A'   CD 0000*              	CALL	SUBLEN		; MATCHB already lands on the first character
  2F8D'   CD 0000*              	CALL	MATCHB
  2F90'   D8                    	RC
  2F91'   C3 0000*              	JMP	PUTCUR
                                
                                ;============================================================
                                ; DISPATCH TABLES -- the messages first, then CMDTAB and ACTTAB.
                                ;============================================================
                                ;============================================================
                                ; MESSAGES -- the bottom row is vim's message line: blank unless something has
                                ; been said on it.  A message is built by successive calls -- EXPRM first, which
                                ; clears the row, then the pieces straight to the terminal.  There is no
                                ; concatenation buffer and none is wanted: the pieces are a name, a flag and a
                                ; number, and each knows how to write itself.
                                ;
                                ; Every message is drawn AFTER the frame (MSGPST, from the main loop), because
                                ; a full repaint blanks the bottom row -- so a message written during the
                                ; command would be wiped by the repaint that same key causes.
                                ;============================================================
                                
                                ;MSGNAM -- open the row and write the file name at HL (a 12-byte FCB field:
                                ; drive, 8 name, 3 type) in quotes, the way vim opens a message: "TEST.TXT".
                                ; A blank name field is vim's "[No Name]".  vim writes a path relative to the
                                ; current directory -- a file in it bare, "../x/VI.MAC" otherwise -- and the
                                ; logged drive is CP/M's current directory, so the drive is written only when
                                ; it is another one: "B:TEST.TXT".
  2F94'                         MSGNAM:
  2F94'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2F95'   3E 22                 	MVI	A,'"'
  2F97'   CD 0000*              	CALL	EXPRM		; clears the row, writes the opening quote
  2F9A'   E1                    	POP	H
  2F9B'   E5                    	PUSH	H		; keep the base: the type field is 9 past it
  2F9C'   23                    	INX	H
  2F9D'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2F9E'   FE 20                 	CPI	' '
  2FA0'   C2 2FAD'              	JNZ	MN_HAS
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-146


  2FA3'   21 2993'              	LXI	H,SNONM
  2FA6'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTSTR
  2FA9'   E1                    	POP	H
  2FAA'   C3 2FF7'              	JMP	MN_END
  2FAD'                         MN_HAS:
  2FAD'   0E 19                 	MVI	C,BF_CURDSK
  2FAF'   CD 0005               	CALL	BDOS		; A = the logged drive, A: = 0
  2FB2'   E1                    	POP	H
  2FB3'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2FB4'   3C                    	INR	A		; the FCB's drive byte is explicit, A: = 1
  2FB5'   BE                    	CMP	M
  2FB6'   CA 2FC4'              	JZ	MN_NAM
  2FB9'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2FBA'   C6 40                 	ADI	'A'-1
  2FBC'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  2FBF'   3E 3A                 	MVI	A,':'
  2FC1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  2FC4'                         MN_NAM:
  2FC4'   E1                    	POP	H
  2FC5'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  2FC6'   23                    	INX	H
  2FC7'   0E 08                 	MVI	C,8
  2FC9'                         MN_NM:
  2FC9'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2FCA'   FE 20                 	CPI	' '
  2FCC'   CA 2FD7'              	JZ	MN_EXT
  2FCF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  2FD2'   23                    	INX	H
  2FD3'   0D                    	DCR	C
  2FD4'   C2 2FC9'              	JNZ	MN_NM
  2FD7'                         MN_EXT:
  2FD7'   E1                    	POP	H
  2FD8'   11 0009               	LXI	D,9
  2FDB'   19                    	DAD	D		; the type field
  2FDC'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2FDD'   FE 20                 	CPI	' '
  2FDF'   CA 2FF7'              	JZ	MN_END
  2FE2'   3E 2E                 	MVI	A,'.'
  2FE4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  2FE7'   0E 03                 	MVI	C,3
  2FE9'                         MN_XL:
  2FE9'   7E                    	MOV	A,M
  2FEA'   FE 20                 	CPI	' '
  2FEC'   CA 2FF7'              	JZ	MN_END
  2FEF'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  2FF2'   23                    	INX	H
  2FF3'   0D                    	DCR	C
  2FF4'   C2 2FE9'              	JNZ	MN_XL
  2FF7'                         MN_END:
  2FF7'   3E 22                 	MVI	A,'"'
  2FF9'   C3 0000*              	JMP	OUTCH
                                
                                ;MSGFLG -- the flags after the name, in vim's order and with vim's spelling:
                                ; [Modified][readonly][New], run together with ONE space before the first of
                                ; them (measured from vim 9.1).  A = 0 leaves [Modified] out, which is the load
                                ; message, where nothing has been changed yet.
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-147


  2FFC'                         MSGFLG:
  2FFC'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0		; B: a flag has been written (the space goes once)
  2FFE'   B7                    	ORA	A
  2FFF'   CA 300F'              	JZ	MF_RO
  3002'   3A 0000*              	LDA	MODF
  3005'   B7                    	ORA	A
  3006'   CA 300F'              	JZ	MF_RO
  3009'   21 299D'              	LXI	H,SMODM
  300C'   CD 3024'              	CALL	MF_PUT
  300F'                         MF_RO:
  300F'   3A 0000*              	LDA	ROFLAG
  3012'   B7                    	ORA	A
  3013'   CA 301C'              	JZ	MF_NEW
  3016'   21 29A8'              	LXI	H,SROM
  3019'   CD 3024'              	CALL	MF_PUT
  301C'                         MF_NEW:
  301C'   3A 0000*              	LDA	MSGNEW
  301F'   B7                    	ORA	A
  3020'   C8                    	RZ
  3021'   21 29B3'              	LXI	H,SNEWM
  3024'                         MF_PUT:
  3024'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  3025'   B7                    	ORA	A
  3026'   C2 3032'              	JNZ	MF_STR
  3029'   06 01                 	MVI	B,1
  302B'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  302C'   3E 20                 	MVI	A,' '
  302E'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  3031'   E1                    	POP	H
  3032'                         MF_STR:
  3032'   C3 0000*              	JMP	OUTSTR
                                
                                ;EMITW -- HL as unsigned decimal, no leading zeros (0 still prints one digit).
                                ; Repeated subtraction of each power of ten, which is all an 8080 has.  B
                                ; carries 'a digit has been printed' so the leading zeros are skipped.
  3035'                         EMITW:
  3035'   C5                    	PUSH	B
  3036'   D5                    	PUSH	D
  3037'   06 00                 	MVI	B,0
  3039'   11 2710               	LXI	D,10000
  303C'   CD 305A'              	CALL	EWDIG
  303F'   11 03E8               	LXI	D,1000
  3042'   CD 305A'              	CALL	EWDIG
  3045'   11 0064               	LXI	D,100
  3048'   CD 305A'              	CALL	EWDIG
  304B'   11 000A               	LXI	D,10
  304E'   CD 305A'              	CALL	EWDIG
  3051'   7D                    	MOV	A,L		; the units digit is always printed
  3052'   C6 30                 	ADI	'0'
  3054'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  3057'   D1                    	POP	D
  3058'   C1                    	POP	B
  3059'   C9                    	RET
  305A'                         EWDIG:
  305A'   0E 00                 	MVI	C,0
  305C'                         EW_LP:
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-148


  305C'   7D                    	MOV	A,L
  305D'   93                    	SUB	E
  305E'   6F                    	MOV	L,A
  305F'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  3060'   9A                    	SBB	D
  3061'   67                    	MOV	H,A
  3062'   DA 3069'              	JC	EW_DN
  3065'   0C                    	INR	C
  3066'   C3 305C'              	JMP	EW_LP
  3069'                         EW_DN:
  3069'   19                    	DAD	D		; one subtraction too many: give it back
  306A'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  306B'   B7                    	ORA	A
  306C'   C2 3072'              	JNZ	EW_PR
  306F'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  3070'   B7                    	ORA	A
  3071'   C8                    	RZ			; a leading zero: write nothing
  3072'                         EW_PR:
  3072'   79                    	MOV	A,C
  3073'   C6 30                 	ADI	'0'
  3075'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  3078'   06 01                 	MVI	B,1
  307A'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;ISEMPT -- Z iff the buffer holds nothing at all: no resident text, and nothing
                                ; spilled behind the window either.  vim's '--No lines in buffer--', shortened.
  307B'                         ISEMPT:
  307B'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	OUTPOS
  307E'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  307F'   B5                    	ORA	L
  3080'   C0                    	RNZ
  3081'   CD 0000*              	CALL	LOGLEN
  3084'   7C                    	MOV	A,H
  3085'   B5                    	ORA	L
  3086'   C9                    	RET
                                
                                ;MSGCTG -- '^G': the file, its flags, and where the cursor is.  DEVIATION: vim
                                ; also gives the file's line total and a percentage of it; no line total is kept
                                ; anywhere here, and counting one means a sweep of the whole file out to EOF and
                                ; a page back -- which would cost the undo region (PGTOPM) as well as the wait.
  3087'                         MSGCTG:
  3087'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,FNAME
  308A'   CD 2F94'              	CALL	MSGNAM
  308D'   3E 01                 	MVI	A,1		; '^G' is where vim shows [Modified]
  308F'   CD 2FFC'              	CALL	MSGFLG
  3092'   CD 307B'              	CALL	ISEMPT
  3095'   C2 309E'              	JNZ	MG_POS
  3098'   21 29C6'              	LXI	H,SNOLIN
  309B'   C3 0000*              	JMP	OUTSTR
  309E'                         MG_POS:
  309E'   21 29B9'              	LXI	H,SLINE
  30A1'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTSTR
  30A4'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CNTLF		; the line feeds before the cursor ...
  30A7'   23                    	INX	H		;   ... so the line it is on
  30A8'   CD 3035'              	CALL	EMITW
  30AB'   21 29C0'              	LXI	H,SCOLM
	MACRO-80 3.44	09-Dec-81	PAGE	1-149


  30AE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTSTR
  30B1'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CBOL		; the byte column within the line, 0-based
  30B4'   23                    	INX	H
  30B5'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  30B6'   CD 3035'              	CALL	EMITW
  30B9'   2A 0000*              	LHLD	CURDCL		; the column a TAB expands that byte to
  30BC'   23                    	INX	H
  30BD'   D1                    	POP	D
  30BE'   CD 0000*              	CALL	CMP16		; the same -> vim writes one number, not two
  30C1'   C8                    	RZ
  30C2'   E5                    	PUSH	H
  30C3'   3E 2D                 	MVI	A,'-'
  30C5'   CD 0000*              	CALL	OUTCH
  30C8'   E1                    	POP	H
  30C9'   C3 3035'              	JMP	EMITW
                                
                                ;FILMSG -- the load message: the file and its flags.  vim adds the line and
                                ; byte totals ('3L, 30B'); the line total is the sweep MSGCTG's note describes.
                                ; A buffer with no file name gets no message at all, as in vim.
  30CC'                         FILMSG:
  30CC'   3A 0001*              	LDA	FNAME+1
  30CF'   FE 20                 	CPI	' '
  30D1'   C8                    	RZ
  30D2'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,FNAME
  30D5'   CD 2F94'              	CALL	MSGNAM
  30D8'   AF                    	XRA	A		; nothing has been changed yet
  30D9'   C3 2FFC'              	JMP	MSGFLG
                                
                                ;WRMSG -- what ':w' says.  vim counts what it wrote ('"TEST.TXT" 3L, 29B
                                ; written'); the counts are the same sweep, so this says only that it happened.
                                ; The name is TFCB's, so ':w OTHER.TXT' names the file it really wrote.
  30DC'                         WRMSG:
  30DC'   21 0000*              	LXI	H,TFCB
  30DF'   CD 2F94'              	CALL	MSGNAM
  30E2'   21 29D8'              	LXI	H,SWRIT
  30E5'   C3 0000*              	JMP	OUTSTR
                                
                                ;MSGPST -- draw the message this key asked for, once the frame is painted, and
                                ; put the cursor back.  The main loop calls it after SCDRAW and MODEMS.
  30E8'                         MSGPST:
  30E8'   3A 0000*              	LDA	MSGWHT
  30EB'   B7                    	ORA	A
  30EC'   C8                    	RZ
  30ED'   47                    	MOV	B,A
  30EE'   AF                    	XRA	A
  30EF'   32 0000*              	STA	MSGWHT
  30F2'   78                    	MOV	A,B
  30F3'   FE 01                 	CPI	MW_FIL
  30F5'   CA 311C'              	JZ	MP_FIL
  30F8'   FE 02                 	CPI	MW_WRT
  30FA'   CA 3122'              	JZ	MP_WRT
  30FD'   FE 04                 	CPI	MW_BIG
  30FF'   CA 3113'              	JZ	MP_BIG
  3102'   FE 05                 	CPI	MW_MEM
  3104'   CA 310D'              	JZ	MP_MEM
  3107'   CD 3087'              	CALL	MSGCTG
